**Verdict:** revise — trust strained, value high, delight clear_hit. 6 blockers, 9 concerns. (`subject.md` was present in the directory; I did not open it.)

**Strongest hit:** the *Tenet* paragraph (line 339). It states the pandemic-release failure in money — "$365 million worldwide against a budget over $200 million, not enough to break even" — names the criticism that the release asked audiences to weigh a movie against a virus, and then closes "He has never conceded the point" without giving him a rebuttal. That refusal is the article's proof it isn't working for its subject. Runner-up: "the method working exactly as designed, which is also the strongest case against it," which concedes that the defense and the indictment are the same fact.

**Highest-priority concern (CRITIC-C1):** not any single error — the direction. I tallied ten places where the record is open or sourcing is soft, and every one resolves toward Nolan or toward the thesis. I searched specifically for a counterexample (did the draft omit anything *favorable* to him?) and found none — no on-record Nolan response to the female-characters charge exists to have been omitted. A lean with no counterexamples is systematic, and it's what should drive the revision rather than the line-level fixes.

Three blockers are critic-specific: the typing linchpin at line 208 is a *reframe* presented as an unprompted answer (the correspondent offered "I have the sense that you don't think of yourself as the most important person on the set" and Nolan corrected it upward); "the one reader with standing to convict him" is false — Mendelsohn published a materially identical charge in NYRB ten days *before* Wilson, and his version ("a sibling of *Memento*'s anguished amnesiac, of Batman, of Oppenheimer") is the direct falsification test for "feeling first" that the piece never faces; and line 373 closes the one live argument it engages in Nolan's favor on a single rave. The other three (Telegraph misattribution, "six films" → four, the 70mm/IMAX 70mm conflation anchoring the ending) are shared fact-checks other perspectives will likely also surface. Nothing needs new research — every repair is already in the packet.

Sources: [NYRB — Mendelsohn on Nolan's Odyssey](https://www.nybooks.com/online/2026/07/17/artful-weaving-odyssey-christopher-nolan/), [Pajiba — Samantha Morton's Circe](https://www.pajiba.com/film_reviews/samantha-mortons-circe-is-the-greatest-feat-of-the-odyssey-.php), [LARB — Know Your Own Men](https://lareviewofbooks.org/article/odyssey-christopher-nolan-women-circe-athena-calypso-penelope/), [Far Out — Nolan and the Bechdel Test](https://faroutmagazine.co.uk/has-christopher-nolan-movie-ever-passed-bechdel-test/)
